🚀 INTRODUCTION: SPLUNK INSTALLATION ON KALI LINUXFollow these structured steps to successfully download, install, and launch Splunk Enterprise on your Kali Linux system.

📦 Step 1: Account Creation & Package SelectionFirst, navigate to the official Splunk website and sign up for a free account. Once logged in, go to the download section, 
          choose Linux, and target the .deb package.Instead of downloading it through the browser, you can copy the wget link from their page to pull it directly into your terminal.
           Command :wget -O splunk-installer.deb "YOUR_SPLUNK_DOWNLOAD_LINK"

📂 Step 2: Navigate to DownloadsOpen your terminal application and switch over to the folder where your installer package was saved.
           Command :~/Downloads

 🛠️ Step 3: Execute the InstallerSince Kali Linux is built on a Debian foundation, use the Debian package manager (dpkg) with root privileges 
              to unpack and install the software.
              Command :sudo dpkg -i splunk-*.deb

⚙️ Step 4: Accept License & Start Splunk ServiceNavigate into the system binaries directory where Splunk was installed. From there, initiate the 
            startup script while automatically accepting the user license agreement.(Note: You will be prompted here to configure your administrator username and password).
             Command : cd /opt/splunk/bin
                       sudo ./splunk start --accept-license

🌐 Step 5: Access the Splunk Web UIOnce the service starts up successfully, you can log into the graphical dashboard using a web browser:On your Kali Linux machine: Open your browser 
            and navigate to:text  http://localhost:8000
  
    Use code with caution.From a host machine browser (Remote Access): Replace localhost with your Kali Linux system's IP address:text
    http://<YOUR_KALI_IP_ADDRESS>:8000
